p identifies the allocated initial-stack span. This is a statement at handoff, before userspace can overwrite the bytes. It makes no statistical claim and no claim that the bytes remain unchanged forever.

The operation should do the following.

Authenticate the retained fs/binfmt_elf.c, relevant auxvec/ELF declarations, and provider source against the retained index. Check the complete local path from buffer declaration through generation, allocation, copy, tag emission, and failure exits.
Establish source and destination correspondence for partial writes as well as success. A failed or interrupted path must not acquire a completed-handoff claim.
Produce the proof and a canonical, integer-only witness describing the provider relation, source anchors, and outstanding actual-exec binding. It must contain neither fabricated seed bytes nor an admission flag.
Independently challenge the argument with changed request length, a substituted provider, a pointer into argv, a mismatched copy source, and a copy failure incorrectly treated as success. These must test the reasoning, not merely checksum rejection.

Use a separate fixed source unit with a 15-minute input gate and at most 60 minutes overall. No new kernel implementation bodies are needed. If native ELF aliases remain essential and unresolved, permit only the specifically named same-commit definition header include/linux/elf.h; stop if further definitions are indispensable. The upstream location is an acquisition lead, not a substitute for the target version. 
GitHub

Success is independent acceptance of this one provenance theorem. STOP on an unresolved provider, tag, conversion, ownership, or failure-path edge. Do not respond by expanding into entropy or FPU internals. Future genuine-owner binding remains necessary; source pins cannot manufacture an actual exec or mapping.

No additional user assurance decision is needed to author this narrow proof under the original OS/loader premise. Accepting stronger entropy guarantees, arbitrary outside payloads, private GCC correctness, or a perpetual integrity interval would require additional evidence or an explicit assurance change.

Full C05/full V03 remain false. Complete channel coverage, C07 lifetime, inventory fit, the intact baseline, and all named V03 controls remain required. All limits, scores, costs marked OPEN_NOT_ZERO, and original authorship and lineage remain unchanged, including Chris R/Clear1nsight, Pro/Codex/Sol Max, PR6321/6029/5864, unpaidmoon/Cursor Grok PR6339, and Douglas R. Colkitt.